Gives the stellux platform swapchains that present to stlxdm, which reads a
picture with the CPU, so the swapchain blits each image to a linear buffer
in host-visible system memory, exported with the image's acquire and
release timelines. stlxdm waits on the acquire point and raises the release
timeline to a latch point once the picture is no longer pending, whether it
latched, was replaced or was released unshown, and to the release point
once it stops reading it, so each commit advances the image's release
point by two, one more than Mesa's common code. FIFO waits for the previous
commit's latch point before committing, MAILBOX commits at once, and
acquire waits until an image not acquired reaches its release point.
Present wait waits for the latch point of the first commit with the present
id asked for or a later one. Each wait on stlxdm sleeps in slices with a
check of the connection between them.

